  "graded": {
    "_doc": "Identity-and-lifecycle I7: the grade inside the signed message (grant_decision_message_graded): after issued_at_ms, a u32 little-endian length and the grade's bytes, only when a grade is named — so every case above, naming none, is unchanged. `service`: the seed's Ed25519 key naming `service` (deterministic, reproduced exactly). `consent`: a consent principal's P-256 key (point_hex the uncompressed X9.63 point, also as SPKI PEM; pkcs8_hex the test key's private half, a fixture and nothing else), one case per consent grade; `sig` is ASN.1 DER ECDSA over SHA-256, which is randomised, so each language recomputes the message and VERIFIES the pinned signature rather than reproducing it. Generated once (ring, 2026-11-17) and pinned; checked by Rust (the_graded_decision_vector_is_the_same_in_every_language), jest and pytest.",
